ing samples from the 2008 Beijing and 2012 London Olympics, using newer, more advanced testing techniques, in an effort to find those who had used performance enhancing drugs (PEDs), but in whom it could not be detected at the time of those Olympics. This was one of the many events affected."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In April 2017 " [:a {:href "/athletes/108047"} "Vasyl Fedoryshyn"] " (UKR) was revealed to have a positive test for turinabol (dehydrochloromethyltestosterone) and stanozolol, and was disqualified, losing his silver medal. Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117053"} "Kenichi Yumoto"] " was advanced to the silver medal position, and Kyrgyzstani wrestler " [:a {:href "/athletes/117054"} "Bazar Bazarguruyev"] " was moved up to a bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "19"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/108116"} "Mavlet Batyrov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "6"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117053"} "Kenichi Yumoto"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117054"} "Bazar Bazarguruyev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KGZ"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KGZ.png"}] "KGZ"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [